; std/canon: the 0/1 protocol every gate in the library rests on.
;
; Two firings, and the module's own cost note says so: the question runs, then
; the protocol prompt reads its answer as INPUT and normalizes it to an exact
; token. Asserting one call here asserted that `$` fires — it does not; it
; assembles the instruction as text at expansion time, which is why the
; WORDING is free and the reading is not.
; expect: calls 2
; expect: clean
; expect: answers
((# std/canon)
 (std-binary "Is the number seven greater than three?"))
